        "transcript": "Alright, thanks both for joining. Quick agenda: pilot dashboards, then SSO, then anything else.\nSounds good. Dashboards first — the inference-cost dashboard looks great, the team has been using it daily.\nLove to hear it. Any numbers looking off?\nNothing so far. A couple of people asked for a filter by GPU type but that's a nice-to-have, not urgent.\nNoted as a nice-to-have then. Okay, SSO. This is the big one blocking wider rollout.\nYeah, that's me. I looked at the Okta side yesterday and it's straightforward — standard SAML 2.0 app.\nExactly, we're a standard SP-initiated flow. You'll need our metadata to set up the app.\nRight. I'll get the Okta SAML app configured on our side this week — it's already on my list for this sprint.\nPerfect. And on my end, I'll send the SAML metadata file and our ACS URL by end of day Friday, June 26th, so you have everything you need.\nGreat, that works. One question — do we enforce SSO for everyone immediately?\nI'd rather not force the whole org through it before go-live. Can we scope enforcement to the pilot group?\nYes, enforcement is per-group. Let's agree: pilot group only until go-live, then we flip it org-wide.\nAgreed. That de-risks it nicely.\nAnything else before we wrap? No? Okay — Dmitri on the Okta app, me on the metadata by Friday. Talk next week.\nThanks Theo, talk soon.",
