        "transcript": "Thanks for making time. I know this project has been stuck behind the security review, so I mostly want to understand where that stands.\nFair. It's taken longer than any of us wanted — the questionnaire touched teams that don't usually review vendors together, and anything touching patient data gets extra scrutiny.\nUnderstood. Is there anything outstanding on our side? More documentation, a call with your reviewers?\nNo, your responses were complete, including the HIPAA and data-handling sections. The remaining answers are drafted internally and I'm waiting on one approval from our platform lead. I expect to close the review out early next week.\nThat's genuinely good news. Oliver, once that lands, what's the path to getting us connected?\nThe moment Nadia signs off, I'll provision the Snowflake service account — read-only on the ANALYTICS schema, exactly as specced. It's a same-day job once the review closes, so I won't put a separate date on it.\nAnd just to confirm scope while we're all here: read-only, ANALYTICS schema only, no raw layer?\nCorrect. Our data governance policy won't allow raw-layer access for external tools — that's where the identifiable lab results live — and honestly you don't need it.\nAgreed, we don't. Once the service account exists we can connect the dbt repo the same day, so the chain unblocks quickly.\nThat's what I'm hoping. We've lost about three weeks; if the connection happens next week we can claw most of that back.\nFrom my side, no further reviews needed after this one. The tool itself was approved — it was the data-sharing terms for the health data that took time.\nGood to know. I won't pile more actions on — the sign-off and the service account are the whole critical path. Anything you need from me?\nNothing right now. If provisioning throws anything weird I'll ping you on Slack.\nPerfect. Let's speak once the account is live. Thanks both.",
        "actionItemsText": "Nadia to close out the security review early next week (waiting on platform lead approval)\nOliver to provision the Snowflake service account (read-only, ANALYTICS schema) the same day security signs off",
        "initial": {
          "proposals": [
            {
              "action": "create_task",
              "draftId": 1,
              "sourceQuote": "The remaining answers are drafted internally and I'm waiting on one approval from our platform lead. I expect to close the review out early next week.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "draftRef": null,
